"Every healer above D-rank gets a passive easing the mental and physical effects of stress."
"Healers above D-rank also get the blessing Twice Life, a doubled lifespan."
"Healers are no good in a fight."
"Nobody trades Healer of Body or Healer of Mind; Mind Healer is super rare."
"An S-rank Healer of Body chosen in the System's first year is nearly 80 and looks 16."
"Healers mend injuries fast, and a superpower injury gets a real healer."
"A couple of Anesidoran Healers do full rejuvenation for those who get on their lists."
"Except rare S-ranks, Healers cannot fix people instantly; spells are long, skills taxing."
"Some D-rank Healers specialize in safely slowing bodily processes for emergencies."
"Systems pick up the slack in cross-species healing; unknown species are hard to treat without one."
"Magical healing brings extreme hunger."
"Corruption wounds are healed by removing the damaged flesh and regrowing it over sessions."
"Human Healers fix injuries but not serious destruction; they cannot regrow an eye."
"Healer triage: injured Avowed first, then local victims of magic, then the regular waitlist."
"Healers are not wasted on criminals, who get human surgeons instead."
"Healers struggle to fix tinnitus caused by a Vocal's attack."
